# Write paths: a deep nested copy (live)

Same assemblage as `examples/writepaths.wcn`. Target is `%cli-live`. Type a
command and press Enter: `jets`, `ocean`, `resize`, or a new fountain name.

`[:Class | path = expr]` rebuilds only the objects on the path. The fountain
sits six levels down; the ocean is a sibling so a deep write can prove it
stays put.

## Schema

```
World = Continent Ocean
Continent = Country
Country = Capital
Capital = Plaza
Plaza = Fountain
Fountain = Int/jets String/name
Ocean = Int/depth
```

## Construction

```
[:World
  [:Continent
    [:Country
      [:Capital
        [:Plaza
          [:Fountain 7 "Triton"]]]]]
  [:Ocean 4000]
]
```

## Methods

```
Fountain::rename = { String/n | [:Fountain | name = n] }

World::moreJets = {
  [:World | continent.country.capital.plaza.fountain.jets = (continent.country.capital.plaza.fountain.jets + 1)]
}

World::renameFountain = { String/n |
  [:World | continent.country.capital.plaza.fountain.name = n]
}

World::deeperOcean = {
  [:World | ocean.depth = (ocean.depth + 100)]
}

World::resize = {
  [:World | continent.country.capital.plaza.fountain.jets = 12, ocean.depth = 5000]
}

World::command = { String/line |
  switch (line)
    "jets" -> { this.moreJets() }
    "ocean" -> { this.deeperOcean() }
    "resize" -> { this.resize() }
    else -> { if (line == "") { this } else { this.renameFountain(line) } }
}

World::boostFountain = { Fountain/f |
  [:Fountain f | jets = (f.jets + 1)]
}

World::label = {
  f = continent.country.capital.plaza.fountain.
  jets = f.jets.
  depth = ocean.depth.
  "Fountain {name} has {jets} jets; ocean {depth} deep.".tpl({String:String "name": f.name, "jets": jets.str(), "depth": depth.str()})
}
```

## Target

```
%cli-live

%init
var assemblage;

function init() {
    assemblage = GameAssemblage.factory();
    wchntConsole.println("jets | ocean | resize | or type a fountain name");
    wchntConsole.println(assemblage.label());
}

%step
function step(line) {
    assemblage = assemblage.command(line);
    wchntConsole.println(assemblage.label());
}
```
